      "notes": "utokyo xarm pick-and-place rev2. Only the action-level semantics is raised: action = joint_target_position. Basis 1 (documentation): the dataset is an xArm 7 demonstration set whose state/action channels are the leader-arm motor commands; this was NOT re-verified against an offline copy of the dataset card on this host. Basis 2 (data behaviour, recomputed over all 7490 rows of data/chunk-000/*.parquet): corr(action,state) mean 0.8656; MAD(action[t],state[t+1])=0.1236 vs MAD(action[t],state[t])=0.1445, a 14% gap, i.e. action leads the state in the next-step direction; both ranges are [-3.141, 3.141], consistent with joint angles in radians but NOT a unit measurement. Known defect carried forward: observation.state[6] and observation.state[7] are constant 0.0 across all rows (placeholder), so state_dim=8 overstates real information and action stays 7D. Units and per-channel roles stay unknown. authority stays SOURCE_DOCUMENTED_PARTIAL (FORMAT_VERIFIED, research snapshot)."
